Where the trees part (s20_k4 group 0: Clarabel 22 nodes, certified; SCS 46, one node open
at the depth limit), each relaxation the SCS search solved, also by Clarabel:
- the nodes that decide the search have relaxation values within about 0.1 of zero on an
  objective scale of 8.4e6; neither solver's exact bound reaches 0 there (Clarabel's are
  1e-3 to 0.2 above it, SCS's 4e-6 to 2.9), so both branch;
- SCS's value at those nodes is off by up to 2.7 from Clarabel's, its sign flipped at four
  of eleven, so its point (which branching and rounding read) is a different point;
- three Shor solves at nodes with fixings took SCS 32,450 to 97,850 iterations (1.5 to
  4.1 s), against about 0.02 s for Clarabel.
So at 1e-6 relative to the scale SCS's point is too coarse for the branching on these
beds, and some nodes are slow for it. Clarabel stays the default.
